@@ -70,6 +70,18 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to :meth:`~rich.console.Console.print` and :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log`. It converts each object to a string, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result as plain text followed by ``end``. Here's an example::
+
+    console.out("foo", "bar", sep=", ", style="bold")
+
+``out`` does not pretty print containers, does not word wrap or crop the output, does not interpret markup, and does not replace emoji codes. Output is written as-is, so the text is not split across lines to fit the terminal width.
+
+``out`` does apply highlighting by default, the same as print. Pass ``highlight=False`` to disable it, or ``highlight=True`` to force it on even if the Console was created with highlighting disabled. The ``style`` argument accepts a basic style, applied the same way as it is by print.
+
+
